> Can a boing be prerecorded in a television show?

onomatopoeic words are allowed to violate phonotactic restrictions so
long as they are pronounceable. In English, that is. Not in Standard
Lojban, though since the Lojban restrictions on consonant cooccurrence
are ill-motivated, I don't see why they need apply to other dialects.

